---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Poll from '../../../components/Poll.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="Poll: How do you mock APIs in React Native?" 
  description="Vote for your preferred API mocking tool for React Native development."
>
  <div class="container mx-auto max-w-[800px] px-5 py-12">
    <div class="mb-8">
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-zinc-900 dark:text-white mb-4">
        How do you mock APIs in React Native?
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">
        Help the community by voting for the API mocking tool you use in React Native projects.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-zinc-50 border border-zinc-200 rounded-xl p-6 md:p-8 dark:bg-zinc-900 dark:border-zinc-800">
      <Poll pollSlug="rn-api-mocking" />
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 text-sm text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400 space-y-2">
      <p>
        <strong>Privacy:</strong> We store a salted SHA-256 hash of your IP plus the poll ID, your option and the time. That's pseudonymous, not anonymous. Deduplication is per IP: one vote per network per poll. Hashes are deleted after 90 days.
      </p>
      <p>
        The voting API runs on Cloudflare Workers with a D1 database. We use IP-based rate limiting (10 requests/minute). Results are shown only after you vote. VPNs and network changes allow extra votes, and a shared IP gets only one vote. Results are informal.
      </p>
      <p class="text-xs">
        <em>Disclosure:</em> The maintainer of this site (Sebastian) is the author of Mockifyer, one of the options in this poll.
        All options are sorted alphabetically, with "Other" listed last.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 border-t border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 pt-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-zinc-900 dark:text-white mb-6">About the Options</h2>
      
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-white mb-2">
            <a href="/tools/miragejs/" class="hover:text-zinc-600 dark:hover:text-zinc-300">MirageJS</a>
          </h3>
          <p class="text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">
            Intercepts fetch and XHR in the JavaScript runtime. In-memory database simulation for building complete frontend applications.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-white mb-2">
            <a href="/tools/mockifyer/" class="hover:text-zinc-600 dark:hover:text-zinc-300">Mockifyer</a>
          </h3>
          <p class="text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">
            Record/replay HTTP mocking for axios and fetch, with JSON mocks in your repo. Supports React Native/Expo via device storage and optional Metro sync. (Built by the site's maintainer.)
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-white mb-2">
            <a href="/tools/mockoon/" class="hover:text-zinc-600 dark:hover:text-zinc-300">Mockoon</a>
          </h3>
          <p class="text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">
            Local mock API server with GUI or CLI. Runs as a separate server; point your app's base URL at it (Android emulator: use 10.0.2.2).
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-white mb-2">
            <a href="/tools/msw/" class="hover:text-zinc-600 dark:hover:text-zinc-300">MSW (Mock Service Worker)</a>
          </h3>
          <p class="text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">
            Network-level HTTP interception using Service Workers in browsers and native Node.js modules. In React Native: MSW 2's msw/native with polyfills ("use at your own risk"). MSW 3 removed it, and @msw/react-native isn't on npm yet.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-white mb-2">
            <a href="/tools/pollyjs/" class="hover:text-zinc-600 dark:hover:text-zinc-300">Polly.js</a>
          </h3>
          <p class="text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">
            Record, replay, and stub HTTP interactions. Built by Netflix, works with multiple adapters including Fetch, XHR, and Node HTTP. Its docs don't cover React Native.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-white mb-2">
            <a href="/tools/prism/" class="hover:text-zinc-600 dark:hover:text-zinc-300">Prism</a>
          </h3>
          <p class="text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">
            Generate mock servers directly from OpenAPI specifications with dynamic examples and validation. Runs as a separate server; point the app's base URL at it (Android emulator: 10.0.2.2).
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 text-sm text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
      <p>
        <strong>Note:</strong> Nock was removed from this poll because it's Node-only: works in Jest, not on device.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 text-center">
      <a 
        href="/polls/" 
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-zinc-600 hover:text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-400 dark:hover:text-white"
      >
        ← Back to all polls
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
